## Executive Summary

Litware Terminal Services (LTS) is a rapidly scaling industrial terminal handling contractor that generated $53.7M in FY2025 revenue with FY2025 adjusted EBITDA of $22.9M [1]. Despite this strong topline growth (21.4% year-over-year), the company manages its $26.1M cost-of-goods-sold base with virtually zero real-time visibility into project costs, fuel consumption, equipment utilization, or production volumes [2]. All five stakeholder interviews conducted in May 2026 independently identified fragmented, paper-based data systems as the organization's single most critical operational bottleneck [3][4][5][6][7].

## Market Context

## Financial Analysis

### Current State

**Revenue and margin performance.** FY2025 revenue reached $53.7M, a 21.4% increase over FY2024's $44.3M [1]. However, total COGS grew 36.1% to $26.1M, outpacing revenue growth and compressing gross margins from 56.7% in FY2024 to 51.5% in FY2025 [1]. The FY2025 adjusted EBITDA of $22.9M represents a 41% margin — well below the 45% budgeted target, resulting in a **cumulative EBITDA variance of negative $2.38M** for the full year [17].

