## Risk Assessment

## Conclusion

Litware Terminal Services is operating a $53.6M+ revenue business with a $26.1M cost base that is managed through paper forms, manual Excel entry, and 30+ day financial reporting lags. This is not a technology preference issue — it is a **structural financial risk**. The FY2025 cumulative EBITDA shortfall of $2.38M against budget [17], combined with COGS growing at nearly twice the rate of revenue [1][18], underscores the urgency of gaining real-time cost visibility.

## Data Enrichment Potential

| Category | Enrichment Opportunity |
|---|---|
| Project-level profitability data | Access to actual job-cost reports would allow direct quantification of project overrun rates, validating the 2–3% COGS reduction assumption with company-specific evidence rather than industry benchmarks. |
| Time-motion study of administrative data entry | A 1-week time study of the office manager, project managers, and CAO's reporting workflow would precisely size the efficiency opportunity, complementing the qualitative findings from stakeholder interviews. |
| Rig connectivity assessment | Detailed analysis of typical connectivity duration, signal strength at operational sites, and existing rig IT infrastructure would inform sync architecture decisions and SaaS platform selection. |
| Historical project overrun analysis | A retrospective analysis of the last 12–24 months of completed projects — comparing estimated vs. actual costs — would directly quantify the cost of delayed visibility. |
| Terminal Handling-specific digital transformation benchmarks | Peer-reviewed ROI studies specific to mid-size U.S. terminal handling contractors would strengthen the financial assumptions beyond the Ridge Industrial case study. |

